adjudication.rationale:
In the diff, `Discourse.Group#findMembers` was changed from returning a promise in the empty-name case (`Ember.RSVP.resolve([])`) to `return ;` (undefined):
```js
findMembers: function() {
  if (Em.isEmpty(this.get('name'))) { return ; }
  return Discourse.ajax(...).then(...);
}
```
So the method is no longer consistently promise-returning. Any existing call site that does `model.findMembers().then(...)` (as the routes did before this commit, and potentially elsewhere outside this diff) would now throw when `name` is blank/empty because `.then` is invoked on `undefined`. That’s a concrete, verifiable behavioral change/defect introduced by the diff.
